BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://comedycalendar.com/
 wp-content/uploads/2026/03/34_Edp-n931yI.png
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://comedycalendar.com/wp-content/uploads/2026
 /03/34_Edp-n931yI.png
UID:p2j5ccaPr19dDGbmzBNT2
SUMMARY:Tony Rock LIVE at Arlington Improv (Saturday Early Show)
DTSTAMP:20260723T104927Z
DTSTART:20260725T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate l
	inks. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Perfor
	mer\nTony Rock is a comedian\, actor\, and producer — the younger brother 
	of Chris Rock — who has built his own legendary career in stand-up and tel
	evision. He hosted HBO’s All Def Comedy\, BET’s Apollo Live\, and co-starr
	ed in CBS’ Living Biblically. He is also the founder of the MyROCK Diabete
	s Foundation. \nEvent Details\nDate: Saturday\, July 25\, 2026 \nTime: 7:0
	0 PM (Doors open 6:00 PM) \nVenue: Arlington Improv\, 309 Curtis Mathes Wa
	y #147\, Arlington\, TX 76018 \nAge Restriction: 18+ \nPrice Range: $25 to
	 $70 per person \nAbout the Venue\nArlington Improv is located in the High
	lands Shopping Center in Arlington\, TX\, across from Torchy’s Tacos. An i
	ntimate comedy club with a full bar\, restaurant\, and Black Dog Pizza Arc
	ade featuring 30+ local craft beers. Seating is assigned based on date of 
	purchase. \nWhat to Expect\nTony Rock delivers a full Saturday night headl
	ining set at Arlington Improv. Expect sharp wit\, personal stories\, and c
	ommanding stage presence from one of comedy’s most seasoned performers. \n
	This is an 18+ event. Doors open at 6:00 PM. Food and beverage service end
	s approximately 45 minutes into the show. All sales are final. \nTicket In
